{
 "_README": [
  "KNOWN-ANSWER world, vendor-neutral 3-hop pivot: alert cites a ticket number -> the ticket names a service account and its only authorised operator -> where the account was used (log server) -> who switched to it on the jump host at the alert time.",
  "The account looks healthy in the directory. The prior monthly run was by the authorised operator; the alert-time run was switched to by mcarrow, who is not authorised.",
  "Answer: true_positive or suspicious. Needles svc-report-gen (hop 1) and mcarrow (hop 3). strict_ops.",
  "Change: the ticket names the jump host the service account is reached through (bastion-02), so the chain from the ticket to the jump host's sudo log is discoverable from the first hop. The alert is unchanged.",
  "Change: the SIEM also holds the bastion-02 sudo log and the db-fin-03 service-account sessions (served for a host or user query on either name), so the log hop is reachable from the SIEM as well as the ticket syslog."
 ],
